WEBVTT

00:00:00.088 --> 00:00:05.843
Offline demo · real API, queue and database · no live provider key

00:00:05.843 --> 00:00:09.209
Create a profile using a bare domain and competitor chips

00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:18.224
The form rejects URLs: store surferseo.com, without https://

00:00:18.224 --> 00:00:20.117
The new profile has no queries until its first run

00:00:20.117 --> 00:00:26.467
Run pipeline returns 202; an RQ worker persists progress and results

00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:31.122
Fake-provider result: 12 queries, 3 recommendations and 750 tokens

00:00:31.122 --> 00:00:38.128
Filters and sorting are server-side; state stays in the URL

00:00:38.128 --> 00:00:44.228
Page two shows the remaining 2 queries

00:00:44.228 --> 00:00:49.399
Not visible narrows the list to missing-visibility opportunities

00:00:49.399 --> 00:00:56.899
Recheck refreshes a single row without reloading the table

00:00:56.899 --> 00:01:03.498
CSV includes every filtered page, with UTF-8 BOM and formula guards

00:01:03.498 --> 00:01:09.265
Orange means not visible; blue means visible. Scores range from 0 to 1.

00:01:09.265 --> 00:01:14.100
Chart axes, controls and content follow the selected theme

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:23.584
Content ideas include priority, rationale, a target query and keywords

00:01:23.584 --> 00:01:26.823
The dashboard now summarizes the persisted profile and completed run

00:01:26.823 --> 00:01:34.408
Frontend reads persisted state; workers own the three-agent workflow

00:01:34.408 --> 00:01:41.924
Validated output leads to completed, partial or failed runs

00:01:41.924 --> 00:01:51.240
Read docs/WALKTHROUGH.md for the ten-minute frontend and backend guide

